<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <a href="/chat">Chat</a> is for messaging the people you work with. Your conversations are listed newest
        first, with a count of unread messages. The Chat item in the menu shows your total unread.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Kinds of conversation">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Direct messages</strong>: just you and one other person.</li>
            <li><strong>Groups</strong>: a named conversation with up to 100 people.</li>
            <li><strong>Channels</strong>: one for each location ("… team", everyone at that location) and one for the
                whole company ("… everyone"). You're added automatically to the channels for the locations you work
                at, so you never need to join them.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Starting a conversation">
        <ol>
            <li>Select <strong>New</strong>.</li>
            <li>Search for people and select them.</li>
            <li>With one person, select <strong>Start chat</strong>. If you've messaged them before, your existing
                conversation opens. With two or more, give the group a name and select <strong>Create group</strong>.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>You can only message people at your company.</FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Group options">
        <FluentText>
            Use the ⋮ menu at the top of a conversation to <strong>Mute notifications</strong>, <strong>Leave group</strong>,
            or, if you started the group or are a manager in it, <strong>Add people</strong> and
            <strong>Rename group</strong>.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
